# Pins for the A1/A2/A3 custom U-Boot port (task-43/44/47/50/51/53/55/58/63 and
# the C1b flash-boot CP15 fix, the A5 vendor-less network bring-up, the A6
# PCIe endpoint reset lines, the D-U1 self-flash commands, the class-1
# slot fallback, the U-0017 environment write-back, the E2 Ethernet driver
# and its F2-a/geometry fixes), the defconfig diet, the E4 v1 web rescue
# (net stack + flash writer API + e2631rescue) and the vendor TOPCRM reset,
# the rescue window fix (task-78) and the env read retry (task-77), the F2 TX
# probe and the bridge-block dump (task-78), the rescue header-name case fix
# (task-78/E4 phase-1, patch 0033), the checkpatch follow-up (a MAINTAINERS
# entry for the port and the e2631net usage page), the cold-boot rescue
# reference-clock fix (patch 0034), the recovery-key rescue trigger
# (patch 0035) and the E4 v2.1 multi-function rescue (patch 0036/0037/0038/
# 0039: the shared slot core + slot writer, the rootfs_data reset and the
# one-shot boot slot, the staged environment write, and the web rescue
# endpoints /slots, /env, /backup, /firmware, /boot, /factory and /console),
# and the task-94 rescue self-checks (patch 0040/0041: zeroed SHA-256
# contexts with upload-window validation, and the output-cursor guard),
# and the E4 v3 rescue endpoints (patch 0042-0049: the defconfig reclaim,
# the 17-byte product comparison, the console raw-length fix, GET /sysinfo
# and /log, POST /integrity, the slot and rootfs backup streams, POST
# /reboot with the blue-LED heartbeat, and the DHCP env keys),
# and the task-92 build fix (patch 0050: the /sysinfo build string needs
# timestamp.h for U_BOOT_DATE/U_BOOT_TIME; found by the first unified v3 build).
#
# Triple pin, same idea as base/commits.env:
#   1. E2631_UBOOT_SHA ......... exact u-boot/u-boot main commit the patches are cut against
#   2. E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_* each patch is content-addressed
#   3. E2631_UBOOT_TREE_SHA ... git tree after "git am" of every patch in uboot-port/patches/;
#                               machine-independent
# The base tree and the post-patch tree are asserted by task-44 CI (uboot-build.yml).
#
# Upstream repo and provenance:
#   u-boot/u-boot, main @ c1958b5f6cce03956d309ce422b5d9f819955d4a (2026-11-19, v2027.01-rc2)
#   The port is GPL-2.0+ and is GPL compatible with U-Boot; see README.md.
#
# Payload budget for later flash stages: secondboot copies header.length bytes from
# mtd0 0x20800, the payload may run to 0xBFFFF and the environment area starts at
# 0xC0000, so u-boot.bin must stay below 0x9F800 bytes (653312, 638 KiB).

E2631_UBOOT_REPO=https://github.com/u-boot/u-boot
E2631_UBOOT_BRANCH=master
E2631_UBOOT_SHA=c1958b5f6cce03956d309ce422b5d9f819955d4a
E2631_UBOOT_BASE_TREE_SHA=62f07967f69e656689266ee1f3e7116cf4b5fd10
E2631_UBOOT_TREE_SHA=fabeca5be8a0c16fb5e7ea6d330560b38429d67c
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0001=1e051c226bb0a5fcd44ded121c73acf03b76b7881d46aad7fd1247c19948c535
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0002=71fdce39af5700bd440f87fbe1d50ce7fe97a1c2ab15a44e009d47af09250003
# 0003: link fix found by the first real build (task-44 CI run 44868198743).
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0003=d16e7b563adc8693ea59e23900870b07a168f44136218d740c3ba49e44c7b395
# 0004: ZTE-variant PL011 register map (A1 console stayed silent with the
# stock ARM offsets; the fix is hardware-proven by the task-45 dual probe).
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0004=ce6a01ef5b0c1c47f213a79a30bc3bb13f0b8cdeec10ebb4395ce988b5e746ca
# 0005: A2 SPI-NAND read path (SPIFC PIO driver + DTS/defconfig). No flash
# writes; the A2 session only runs "mtd list"/"mtd read".
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0005=43dcac25fe9c57e36898bcdbe7e4462c7bd865826bd7b72e389c7fa5d562f70f
# 0006: A3 slot-aware boot (e2631boot command + ATAGS bootcmd). Read-only:
# the command scans both firmware slots and boots the winning uImage via bootm.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0006=35ba682af0a5b5c71ff41c94c104a99afca609087c3bf42e4721370d6dde26ca
# 0007: A3 read-only environment block (ENV_IS_IN_MTD at 0xC0000, saveenv
# compiled out) plus the env_mtd_load() uninitialised-pointer fix.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0007=bf54aa985373952cac402dafacc2b49f9876993b8150541ec13a10d94f800f97
# 0008: C1a pre-flash blocker - board_late_init() now points bootm at a valid
# ATAGS buffer (board was never setting gd->bd->bi_boot_params; boot_prep_linux
# data-aborted on the ATAG_MEM write). Static assertions pin the buffer between
# the DRAM base and the kernel load address.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0008=d75f809f91f7cfcca08de5b04a6ec4c77e77df6f64c14a9f73544515a7c20748
# 0009: keep the env location name when CONFIG_CMD_SAVEENV is off, so the log
# says "Loading Environment from MTD... OK" instead of "<NULL>" (C1a read the
# <NULL> as "env-mtd is not live"; the MTD load itself had succeeded).
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0009=4bf75d5afe821f0e58dce01c88fa326a3adf4a33c708f5d7c4712d243ad14e91
# 0010: link at the product entry. secondboot copies the payload to
# 0x47F00000 and jumps there with blx (evidence/uboot-re-20261115.md); the
# port is not position independent (CONFIG_POSITION_INDEPENDENT off, relocate.S
# assumes run address == link address), so TEXT_BASE is 0x47F00000 now. The
# vendor-console RAM chain loads the same image at 0x47F00000 (vendor U-Boot
# relocates itself to the top of DRAM, so the link area is free).
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0010=57ce9d808cc771854bb68b03020d9da854d24b0bd621b5971b882e342ff079a0
# 0011: normalise CP15 before the Linux hand-off (C1b-1 flash-boot hang).
# The flash chain skips the vendor entry/cleanup passes; the patch turns the
# standard entry normalisation back on (CONFIG_SKIP_LOWLEVEL_INIT off) and
# runs the vendor-order CP15 cleanup as the last step before bootm. The
# e2631soc command prints SCTLR/CLIDR/TTBR0/VBAR/ACTLR before and after the
# same code path. No PL310/SCU writes: the vendor does none either.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0011=98aa4b3914ff1741e0621116b4d630ab43f448d7d0ca31496c2001e815b51095
# 0012: bring up what the vendor board_eth_init() does and the flash chain never
# ran (A5). The four internal PHYs and both PCIe links stay silent otherwise:
# the kernel's clk driver assumes the bootloader has already programmed the
# network PLL/SerDes (clk-zx279128s.c:8-10), and no kernel driver touches
# 0x94000008/0x94000050/0x94000054, 0x94100010, 0x9FE00000 or 0x9A100004.
# The patch replays the vendor sequence byte for byte (fractional PLL, SerDes
# table, CRM2 clock select, 0x9400004c/0x9A100004, the 0x9400000c mux the vendor
# Ethernet probe selects) plus the pinmux and the eight GPIO outputs. The
# register set was trimmed against a pre/post dump of the two chains: the pinmux
# is six whole board-table words after the three ORs, the ten input entries need
# no write (DIR already clear out of reset), and the CRM2 writes that are
# already identical on our chain are not replayed. e2631refclk prints
# before/after of the seven clock registers and never boots. Flat GPIO 53 (the
# H3600-era pcie0 reset-gpios guess) is deliberately NOT driven.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0012=9c075c60f5cd6282e8b507d7ee0e02b4fc68544d0f55f4d1b4c43a8f187ed87b
# 0013: the two late GPIO drives of zte_gpio_init() (A6). After the board-table
# replay the vendor walks the table again and drives the enabled output entries
# at table index 51 and 50, pins 2 and 51, to 1 although the table says 0. They
# are the remaining state difference in the A5 pre/post dump, and with them low
# the kernel sees both PCIe root ports but no endpoint (no 14c3:7906/790a, so
# mt7915e never binds), while the vendor-booted chain sees them. Likely the two
# endpoint reset/power enables. The vendor drives pin 2, waits 4 ms (mdelay(4)
# right before loop B), then drives pin 51; the patch keeps that gap and drives
# them high after the table replay.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0013=f6d52c559973dad5cc4e375f72e7dd3ce57b63c8b15f1ca95e5bb011346d5f2c
# 0014: self-contained flash/verify/slot commands (D-U1). e2631flash is the
# only MTD writer (e2631verify is read-only and e2631slot reuses e2631boot's
# scan routine). Sources are staged in a 1 MiB RAM bounce buffer, so the
# flash-to-flash update never reads the destination while erasing it.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0014=0bfb4302fec14b6d0d2549cebe4a1ddf311bd50f044849d0bdaf09c1ed943110
# 0015: CONFIG_CMD_MTD_WRITE (bool, default y) gates the raw mtd write and
# erase subcommands. This defconfig disables it, so e2631flash is the only
# code in the image that calls mtd_write()/mtd_erase().
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0015=84bfc65f5bb335d5a6d33b93ccfb8e367e210d0af155ddc6ab82eb14fa6c8f3b
# 0016: class-1 slot fallback. cspboot validates the kernel of the slot it
# selected and boots the other slot when that uImage is unusable; e2631boot
# now retries the other slot exactly once (header read, magic/type/OS/
# compression, header CRC, size window, short read, data CRC). The retry is
# stateless: no flash write, no environment change, the serial selection rule
# is unchanged and e2631slot keeps sharing the same scan and pick code.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0016=7838e8a22dd46996c9ccb31f9fe116e194641d2a26f548e9854548bfefc62461
# 0017: whitelisted environment write-back (U-0017). e2631env is the only env
# writer in the image: env/mtd.c keeps .save NULL and CONFIG_CMD_SAVEENV stays
# off, so the generic env_mtd_save() path never exists. save runs the same
# five steps as e2631flash (bad-block precheck, erase, verify all-0xFF, write,
# read back and compare) at the frozen CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET/SIZE, refuses any
# non-e2631_*/bootdelay change, restores the bootcmd/bootargs/memsize/
# versioninfo snapshot before exporting, checks 0xE0000..0xFFFFF stays blank
# before and after the write, and leaves the block alone when nothing changed.
# The D-U1 allowlist therefore covers exactly four MTD writer sites in three
# helper functions (e2631_write_range, e2631_erase_range, e2631_env_write_block).
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0017=da21478e0fe7c53fdf14f59e81ea3da86733b63998926f25e84b3675f96eca0d
# 0018: the clause-22 MDIO bus for the four integrated PHYs (MDIO 10..13).
# The bus is passive until the first transfer, when it runs the patch-0012
# clock/SerDes hook once so an "mii" command works before eth start.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0018=9a1e079b740d8f253f5c4c9a323a618a5820b8100ccbcff56fae84557d215a9c
# 0019: switch, traffic manager and DMA setup (register map header plus the
# table/DMA/BMU/switch/MAC initialisation the Linux driver uses on the same
# silicon).  The 16 MiB buffer-pool arena at 0x45000000 is reserved here.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0019=3e615397a428781683f753f42374a74b100d739819de64a63408616b557b4a3f
# 0020: the U-Boot Ethernet driver on top of that setup: fixed 16 MiB DMA
# arena, polled TX/RX through the BMU buffer pool, lan1 (switch port 2, PHY
# 12), e2631net debug command.  e2631flash refuses a RAM source that overlaps
# the live arena, and e2631verify refuses to compare it.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0020=d8b9eb9f93125798c4d17a2fc09b621a5d9f139706263dcbd9160ba6b3e1416a
# 0021/0022: checkpatch follow-up.  0021 adds one MAINTAINERS entry covering
# the board, the SoC support directory, the Ethernet/MDIO/SPI drivers, the
# DTS, the defconfig and the command docs; 0022 adds doc/usage/cmd/e2631net.rst
# for the E2 command.  No code changes in either patch.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0021=c66643e1eca8c5cc2313e0136636b0ea22822f38f7207236b41786ba93ab7976
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0022=680435c34a4b6ca5154debb0ace1caea7fd7000641e5e572c6477f22b6959b72
# 0023: F2-a fix after the E2 session (task-69 item 1). The send path never
# dropped a frame silently again: a BMU allocation failure prints the reason,
# the one buffer the frame needed and the BMU state, and a request that times
# out stays pending so the late buffer is collected on the next call (kernel
# pending-retry semantics, zx279128s-main.c zx_bmu_alloc_bp()).
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0023=e38d0545d0463101e19a26760a29fc7ebbc6b8b5782cce836ffc9d5e725c87d3
# 0024: defensive geometry (task-69 item 2). Compile-time asserts tie the
# uImage staging address, the kernel copy window and the DMA arena together;
# a 3,491,146-byte staged image ends at 0x4235454A, 46.8 MiB below the arena
# (the card-era 0x4554xxxx figure was a hex conversion error; see README).
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0024=8bf4e048b1726c795b04ebb92ec361e7a91814fded24f83b3e1432a88b0f79e1
# 0025: defconfig-only space fix (task-69). CONFIG_MMC=n also clears BLK, and
# BLK is what made EFI_LOADER (default y on armv7) and BOOTSTD (default y
# if BLK) come back; FS_FAT/FAT_WRITE followed from EFI_LOADER. Dropping
# the four subsystems removes 56 =y symbols (nothing added) and the bootefi/
# eficonfig/bootflow/bcb commands; e2631boot, e2631flash, e2631env, net,
# bootm, MTD and dhcp/tftp/ping/mii are untouched.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0025=af158e9fb09bc1853a0ff7bf5a32d7201b9ebf8dd04a02a1087e0cccf76218d4
# 0026: E4 v1 (task-72) - the minimal TCP stack and DHCP server taken from
# bl-mt798x-dhcpd (GPL-2.0, commit e4cf4dc7) and adapted to the legacy U-Boot
# net API of this tree: public include/net/mtk_tcp.h, private net/mtk_tcp_priv.h,
# the DHCP server without its console command, arp_wait_clear(), the
# CONFIG_MTK_TCP PROT_TCP hook in net/net.c, net/Kconfig and net/Makefile.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0026=727b6f1f48db406c6c24ffc86c101fefad4780f7b93ad17ef424b5d5958b9682
# 0027: E4 v1 - e2631flash exposes its five-step erase/blank/write/readback/
# compare job through e2631flash.h, so the rescue page reuses the single safe
# writer instead of growing a second MTD write path (D-U1 allowlist unchanged).
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0027=e6a52064d33e0fe43570462f10764e8c41e03d6bfc800918f951aa4db9a5b2a0
# 0028: E4 v1 - the e2631rescue command: DHCP + a minimal HTTP server on lan1,
# gzip-embedded rescue page (task-73 asset), GET /, GET /status, POST /flash
# (raw 655360-byte body, SHA-256 contract, structural header checks), and the
# five-step write of the whole U-Boot area mtd0 0x20000..0xC0000 (655360
# bytes). The write source is the image base (file[0] lands at flash 0x20000)
# and the erase/write/compare windows are identical; compile-time asserts tie
# the end to CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET. Nothing is written before a validated image
# and the X-E2631-Confirm: write header are present; the env and reserved
# sectors are never touched; no automatic reboot.  task-78 fixed the window
# and the three source pointers before any device write.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0028=ef442221929cfcd817f84784cd6f83cb9576a7e76652831b829057ca3865dd21
# 0029: task-76 - replace the placeholder reset_cpu() with the vendor reset
# (print "resetting ...", wait 50 ms, store 1 in TOPCRM+0x44 = 0x94000044); the
# BootROM then reloads secondboot and U-Boot. No MTD write path added.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0029=a016c9dfc1a62e1f8721d603bd773437f273b204f46ffeb1794c61fdfbfe81ea
# 0030: task-77/U-0031 - env_mtd_load() retries the whole MTD read/import
# cycle up to three times before falling back to the default environment, and
# on the final failure prints the mtd0 offset, the stored and computed CRC32,
# the buffer CRC32 and the first 64 bytes, so a bad env read (the thin E4
# build once lost the vendor ethaddr this way) can be diagnosed from the
# serial log.  The environment stays read-only here; no flash write is added.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0030=5c171e5965b295df0dc16c06eb49684cd7504d1a97bcf06de1b02682ef56994a
# 0031: task-78/F2b - the TX probe for the F2 hunt.  The TX descriptor variant
# (directed-egress queue 40 + port vs the vendor's queue 0, word 3 bit 0) is a
# run-time knob whose default stays the kernel descriptor; e2631net tx sends
# broadcast probe frames through the same send path as DHCP/TFTP and prints
# the DMA doorbell/completion, the hardware descriptor index, the last
# descriptor, the traffic manager status, the per-port MAC transmit counters
# and the bridge block's egress masks; e2631net sbrg allow restores the CPU
# port's egress mask.  Diagnostic only: no flash write path is added and the
# default TX behaviour is unchanged.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0031=d431d1fb805da056a2ac2f851f31cf45f14e6fc37de8d20d5ff95023af001fc3
# 0032: task-78/F2c - the F2 root cause.  The U-Boot port wrote BIT(17) to the
# switch forward control (0x1cc000) where the kernel driver writes 17
# (zx279128s-main.c "Switch: enable forwarding") and the vendor bootloader
# writes the same 17 from its switch init (payload 0x47f310c8, called from the
# Ethernet init at 0x47f2ff6c).  With BIT(17) the switch never forwards a frame
# the CPU hands to a switch port: the TM consumes the descriptor and reports the
# completion, but the MAC counters and the wire stay empty.  The patch also adds
# e2631net bmu (TM buffer window, BMU pool, DMA ring window and the forward
# control) and reports the BMU block plus raw BUF_ID the probe saw; 0x1fc is
# printed as dma err, and the SBRG dump is read-only with 'allow' replaying the
# reset masks.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0032=8d1d11fdeae32fef0e2cccd364ffe1cad0dcaf3fc38f90728f8b5250e68d58a5
# 0033: task-78/E4 phase-1 - the rescue HTTP header names were compared
# case-sensitively: rescue_name_is() lowered only the received line, so the
# mixed-case literals the callers pass (Content-Length, X-E2631-SHA256,
# X-E2631-Confirm) could never match and every POST /flash answered 400
# "unsupported request" while GET / and GET /status kept working.  Both sides
# are folded now, the helpers live in the dependency-free e2631http.h, and
# uboot-port/tests/rescue_headers_test.c replays a captured mixed-case request
# on the host in CI.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0033=5657f596688825f2111fd3fea3108fbe93e2973231f28947d0c2faa56d2e21ca
# 0034: task-78/E4 cold boot - e2631rescue can be the first command after a
# cold flash boot, before e2631boot has run.  The network reference clocks and
# the SerDes lanes are then still off, the internal PHYs do not answer MDIO and
# phy_startup() times out (-110), so the rescue reports "no usable Ethernet
# device".  do_e2631rescue() now calls the idempotent
# e2631_net_refclk_init() before net_init()/eth_init(), and CI asserts the call
# stays inside do_e2631rescue().
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0034=eef4625c0e3689acf7055de3636b2edc5a7a4d0f4e89cc0c3ee0161fc0c1e986
# 0035: task-82 recovery keys - holding the reset key (flat GPIO 18, bank 1
# bit 2) or the mesh key (flat GPIO 20, bank 1 bit 4) through
# board_late_init() overrides bootcmd to e2631rescue in RAM only.  Active
# low, external pull-ups, raw DATA reads (no DM_GPIO); the kernel's old
# "hold reset through boot" factory-reset gesture is replaced by the rescue.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0035=9bb04c566e4319debba7a32509a2d07e37e45fe5166ca8229eef75c92d0734e4
# 0036: E4 v2 module C (task-84) - the shared slot core and the slot writer.
# e2631_slotcore.{c,h} is the Linux-side e2631-fwslot logic compiled into
# U-Boot (package parse, identity, guard, slot scan/verify, version-header
# stamp); it stays byte-identical to the kit copy in tests/native/uboot, and a
# host fixture in CI compiles it against the shims.  e2631fwslot.{c,h} is the
# MTD shim: the only code that erases/writes a firmware slot, on top of the
# same five-step pattern (bad-block precheck, erase, write, read back, verify
# the scanned slot).  No rescue code touches MTD directly.
# 0037: E4 v2 - the rootfs_data reset and the one-shot boot slot.
# e2631factory.c erases and blank-checks the rootfs_data partition only (the
# partition must be exactly 0x3360000/0x4A0000, otherwise the module refuses);
# the DTS gains only that one fixed partition so the name resolves.  The
# e2631_next_slot override lets the web rescue pick slot 0/1 for the next
# boot in RAM only (never written to the environment).
# 0038: E4 v2 - the staged environment write for the web rescue.
# e2631env exposes begin/poll/end over the same frozen env block and
# whitelist/snapshot rules as e2631env save; one key per request, five-step
# write, and the writer stays inside e2631env.c.
# 0039: E4 v2.1 - the web rescue grows the multi-function endpoints.
# GET /slots, /env and /backup; POST /firmware (validate/write with guards),
# /boot, /factory and /env (one key), and /console (one command, 4 KiB tail).
# The rescue only schedules the slot/env/factory writers through their state
# machines; the four MTD writer modules and the boot path keep their order.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0036=0496364d698de5e4e042d07654f1ed7e1aba9235d4130ba5205c58f0a85f24cb
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0037=4e71152c02de9fce7a8165dee5e29b97a05999edd37e29d3aafd9d68eb75f5f3
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0038=8f39cbbb3cd37099167b4cb0aa07ac84436f3802fd9db6e6b54bac80502661f9
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0039=41a80fc113357ed3abdf7647ada25d6b85edf3f35f9c82798bca9ca706e8a5af
# 0040: task-94 defensive fix - every SHA-256 in the rescue runs through an
# explicitly zeroed sha256_context, and rescue_sha256() validates the
# (base, maxlen) of the two upload windows before hashing, so a corrupted
# pointer stops the request instead of producing a bad digest.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0040=d274ff0f586caefa0a7fb77caa59e0e515af02829062639129a89a537077112e
# 0041: task-94 defensive fix - rescue_fmt() works inside a registered
# buffer range and refuses to render once the output cursor leaves it;
# /status and /slots answer 500 error=output cursor corrupted instead of
# walking a wild pointer into vsnprintf().
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0041=cf03f0e239e286551cb24f619c8d45fc4fd27d4b74a8d7df7164b6e953c64e1b
# E4 v3 (task-90): the v3 contract delta of 2026-11-28.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0042=6f322294061909aa36c74de87c8f618d6fb019da47775e74b84ec422947516c8
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0043=5bbe5d2b6b91384de357c49b94c9f5610713512a860385cdbc679e24a0e9068b
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0044=aa0e9b0a69e33bfbf077e0023dde0bdba686ca5bec428de4c1be513bf03e63ac
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0045=65a8751b1d6daa42d54d3ffe5271f0a138754aeb79bfd851126852b66ad85166
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0046=746fead6b0a265de3b7684cff16cc7d1c90bf15fc91c3dd49ce36b4ad634bc0b
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0047=1960f78df83062ec95d93115162ad93a2d139813a97961d461de21393badc4e3
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0048=5f5dba995c699f03189e7fd1e0eb6906790d8afdb97e679eb9b2bc0820d5e0b0
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0049=ba15e88c0095e65e934e1fb8829e988e8f1e7c3fb9d9f5b6a5d74367af67d904
# 0050: task-92 build fix - e2631rescue.c includes timestamp.h for the
# U_BOOT_DATE/U_BOOT_TIME pair reported by GET /sysinfo.
E2631_UBOOT_PATCH_SHA256_0050=cbdaed605b5ddb5f958d8290c9b55250722bb3fbbcb09ccfc5d24c9c02d30791
E2631_UBOOT_PAYLOAD_MAX=0x9F800
# task-90 size budget: E4 v3 starts from the task-84 v2.1 build (405368
# bytes, run 46109519805).  Patch 0042 reclaims the fdt and tftp command
# packages (measured 12,380 bytes) and the v3 endpoints are bounded so that
# the image still leaves at least 240 KiB below the hard 653,312-byte
# ceiling: the gate is size <= 653312 - 245760 = 407552 bytes.
E2631_UBOOT_SIZE_BASELINE=405368
E2631_UBOOT_HEADROOM_MIN=245760
E2631_UBOOT_HARD_LIMIT=653312
E2631_UBOOT_TEXT_BASE=0x47F00000
# Fixed build epoch (task-69 item d).  The workflow exports this as
# SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, so U-Boot's filechk_timestamp.h (Makefile:2327-2351)
# embeds this constant instead of the CI clock, and it replays the patches
# with `git am --committer-date-is-author-date`, so the version token no
# longer depends on the build time.  Value: the committer timestamp of the
# pinned base commit c1958b5f (2026-11-19T15:44:39Z).  Two consecutive CI
# runs of the same pins then produce byte-identical u-boot.bin and mtd0.
E2631_UBOOT_SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=1795103079
